Audience: {{ scope.audience }}
Length preset: {{ preset.name }} — target {{ preset.target_words.min }}–{{ preset.target_words.max }} words TOTAL
Max sections: {{ preset.section_budget.max_sections }}
Max subsections per section: {{ preset.section_budget.max_subsections_per_section }}
Target words per subsection: ~{{ preset.section_budget.words_per_subsection }}

Design a COMPREHENSIVE, AUTHORITATIVE outline in the style of a Nature Review or a Very Short
Introduction. It must let a reader learn almost everything important about the (narrowed) topic.

Requirements:
- Follow a scholarly arc: Introduction; Historical background; Key concepts / definitions;
  Prior work; Current state and debates; Methods/approaches; Open problems; Synthesis; Future work;
  Conclusions; References. Include only sections the (narrowed) scope genuinely warrants.
- Every section MUST have 2–{{ preset.section_budget.max_subsections_per_section }} subsections.
  Each subsection has a stable slug `id`, a `title`, a `purpose`, `key_questions`, and a
  `target_words` of about {{ preset.section_budget.words_per_subsection }} (more for central
  material, fewer for minor points).
- For long documents ({{ preset.target_words.max }} words), go one level deeper: give a subsection
  `children` (sub-subsections) when it covers several distinct ideas. Every LEAF (a subsection with
  no children) is written by its own dedicated generation, so finer leaves give more, deeper
  coverage. Parents contribute only a heading; a parent's `target_words` is the sum of its children.
- A section's `target_words` is the sum of its leaf targets plus a short lead.
- Choose the number of sections so the TOTAL of all `target_words` lands within
  {{ preset.target_words.min }}–{{ preset.target_words.max }} words. Depth per section matters
  more than the number of sections.
- Each section needs a stable slug `id`, `purpose`, `key_questions`, `target_words`,
  `source_domains` (subset of arxiv, pubmed, exa, tavily, wikipedia, web) and acyclic `depends_on`
  section ids. Independent sections (empty `depends_on`) run in parallel; Synthesis/Conclusions
  depend on the rest.
- Include a References section with `target_words` 0 and no subsections.
